    "done_when": "Every clause of the plan's s14 done-when holds. In reckon/metadata_index.py build_index compares a file's stat identity without its device against the persisted entry's recorded signature first; when they match and the row is complete the row is reused with no read of the file; when they differ today's digest path runs unchanged. Also remove the third element _reuse_covered returns, which every caller discards (index_rows binds it and never reads it; _covered_files and reckon/resources.py read only the first element), together with the docstring paragraph describing it, so _reuse_covered returns the covered set and its directories as before the re-scan section; reckon/resources.py needs no change. A new tests/test_a_restart_reuses_rows_by_stat_identity.py builds and persists a temporary project, clears the process memo to stand in for a restart, builds again, and proves with its own control each: (1) the second build calls _content_digest zero times and reuses every row; control: restore digest-first and the count equals the file count. (2) a file whose bytes change is parsed again; control: compare the signature without its modification time and a same-size edit is reused stale. (3) a file rewritten with the same bytes and a new modification time is reused through the digest with one digest and no parse; control: skip the digest fallback and it is parsed again. (4) a persisted entry whose recorded device differs is still reused by signature; control: compare the full signature including the device and every file is digested. Each control is applied, run, logged with its failing id and reversed in a trap, and git status --porcelain afterwards lists only the .venv and .env links. The tests covering the metadata index pass, and tests/test_every_module_fits_a_worker_window.py shows no new failure beyond the reckon/roadmap.py one present at base, run with -n 4 at most and a per-run --basetemp; the coordinator runs the population at merge. Every log sits under the run directory with a revision header naming the revision it ran at and ends in EXIT=, on the fleet allocation and not the login node. Write status complete as your very last action and run nothing after it.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Reuse an unchanged file's persisted index row by its stat identity before reading and hashing the file",
